PRIOR ART AND REFERENCES
========================

The design of setpoint was informed by the following projects. No code was copied
from any of them unless stated otherwise.

gguf-parser-go (Apache-2.0)
    Static GGUF memory estimation. Its estimation formulas were read as reference
    while implementing setpoint's own budget model.
    https://github.com/gpustack/gguf-parser-go

llama-optimus (MIT)
    Flag search over llama.cpp parameters using Optuna. Informed the search space
    definition; setpoint uses a different search strategy.
    https://github.com/BrunoArsioli/llama-optimus

llama-swap (MIT)
    Model process orchestration and OpenAI-compatible proxying. Informed the
    configuration and process management design planned for phase 2.
    https://github.com/mostlygeek/llama-swap

Zeus (Apache-2.0)
    GPU energy measurement methodology, including the documented sampling
    limitations of NVML power readings.
    https://ml.energy/zeus/

mixtral-offloading (MIT), MoE-Infinity (Apache-2.0), KTransformers (Apache-2.0),
PowerInfer (MIT)
    Expert caching, activation-aware prefetching and contextual sparsity research
    referenced for phases 4 and 6.

llama-moe-cache / FATE (AGPL-3.0)
    Published benchmarks and the cross-layer plus temporal expert prediction
    approach were referenced as prior art. Because of its license, no code from
    this project has been or may be incorporated into setpoint.
    https://github.com/ongunm/llama-moe-cache
